      "thinking": "Tracing the incident: the cache pointed to the wrong port, causing lookups to fail and latency to spike from 26ms to 190ms. The fallback path still returns correct results, but I realize the real problem is that the fallback compute path itself is quadratic\u2014recomputing sums and selections in nested loops\u2014so losing the cache shouldn't cause a 7x slowdown unless that underlying algorithm is inefficient.\n\nThis makes the shop's performance dangerously dependent on the cache being available; the real fix is making average_spend_per_item and typical_spend_per_item linear (or O(n log n)) so correctness and speed don't hinge on caching. I want to check the tests to match the existing code style before implementing.\n\n",
